35,2,1,talk,May,,"The pilots were clean, but the audits show waiting, not paying, is the real time thief.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""May"",""self"":true,""raw"":""May: The pilots were clean, but the audits show waiting, not paying, is the real time thief.""}]}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The late-turn pool is empty. Overtime is covering everything, including maintenance. We are running on fumes, not capacity.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The audits confirm my fear: we lose time waiting for connections, not paying. The mid-city runs are slower, but platforms clear fine.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The minutes show the ferry and rail offices never agreed on data terms. The pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows a ring-fenced grant, but operating subsidies are trimmed. Ticketing fees now exceed paving budgets. Recurring costs are eating our capital.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, so the mid-city corridor is just a perception problem? That makes the bus plan look like a waste of money.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, not quite. The corridor is slow, but the real killer is the empty late-turn pool. We can’t staff the extension without burning out the few crews left.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, it’s not just perception. The surface route is genuinely slower, but the platforms aren’t the bottleneck. We need to fix the connections, not just the lanes.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that empty pool explains the stalls. But @May, the data terms are still missing. We cannot promise a date without the ferry and rail agreeing.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the empty pool confirms the recurring costs are bleeding us dry. We cannot fund new services while ticketing fees eat the capital.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, if the data terms are missing, the integrated fare platform is a fantasy. We can’t build a single account on a broken handshake.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, precisely. And @Shizue, the maintenance contract has spare capacity, but the roster books show the late-turn pool is empty. We can’t staff the extension without burning out the few crews left.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, the data gap is real, but the time loss is in the connections. We must fix the flow, not just the ticketing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you are right. Without that handshake, the platform is just a dream. We must respect the ground and the people who must agree.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, the recurring fees are a silent tax. We cannot fund new infrastructure while the old ticketing contracts drain our capital.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, so we’re stuck? No data, no crews, no money. Which plan actually survives this mess?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, not stuck, just honest. The lift contract has spare capacity. We can fix station access without breaking the crew or the budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that sounds promising. But if the real loss is waiting for connections, does fixing station entrances actually save passengers time?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the ground is honest. The shells hide voids, but the lift crews are ready. We can trust the access upgrades.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the lift contract’s spare capacity is the only line item that doesn’t bleed us dry. It respects the ledger’s limits.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
