63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, the ground is honest. The shells hide voids, but the lift crews are ready. We can trust the access upgrades.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the access upgrades respect the ledger’s limits. They use the spare capacity without triggering the recurring fee trap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, the pilots proved the late-night idea works, but the rosters are empty. I’m voting C. The access upgrades are the only plan that doesn’t break the bank or the crews.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, agreed. The rosters are empty, so D is impossible. A is blocked by data gaps. B ignores the connection bottleneck. C is the only viable path. I vote C.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The audits show connections are the bottleneck, but C is the only plan that fits our current constraints. I vote C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, I am glad we found a path that respects the ground and the people. The lift crews are ready, and the data gaps do not block this. I vote C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, the ledger confirms C is the only choice that doesn’t trap us in recurring debt. I vote C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
